To apply a neoclassical style to the region of the green grass in this image, you can follow these steps:

1. Isolate the green grass region using a mask or selection tool.
2. Apply a neoclassical filter or texture to the selected region.
3. Adjust the contrast and brightness to enhance the neoclassical style.
4. Add details such as geometric patterns or columns to the grass to further emphasize the neoclassical style.
5. Blend the edges of the affected region with the surrounding areas to ensure a seamless transition.

Here's an example of what the instruction might look like in a text-based image editing software:

```
// Apply neoclassical style to green grass region
selection green-grass;
filter neoclassical-style;
adjust-contrast 50;
adjust-brightness 25;
effect geometric-patterns 10;
effect columns 5;
blend-edges smooth;
```

This instruction assumes that the image editing software supports the named filters and effects mentioned. The exact commands may vary depending on the software being used.

